{
  "case": "serialize-001-main-drawio",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a710.2 L801; \u00a710.1 L737",
  "derivation": "Vendored unchanged from the JS lot-4 seal (seal.json SHA-256 2182fdfa57e862f50e2c07261dc2864c3e475cd33c249db6d28dd957b76ccddf), case file SHA-256 d6fbcf56b04df732543f3bd1400c91a701746f0a08a49486075b0a4b94a46e8a; values owned by that seal (harmonization \u00a73; parity sync PS-H19). JS derivation: One diagram per page in page order with the IR page ID and name; one cell per IR record in emission order; vertices carry the IR name/text, edges their IR source/target; top-level cells hang on the diagram layer. UTF-8 without BOM, LF only, no indentation, no compression, short empty elements, the pinned attribute order, no timestamp or random mxfile attributes; digest = SHA-256 of the returned bytes; the Result carries the preparation identity/revision, the prepared loss entries, idMap and capability. Fails against: Regenerating IDs, dropping labels, compressing despite compression none, CRLF newlines, a modified/etag attribute, another attribute order, a digest of something other than the bytes, or a report that drops the losses.",
